milestones.description:
Using the symmetric matrix
A=\begin{pmatrix}1&1&m\\1&2&n\\m&n&3\end{pmatrix}
with m\in[-\sqrt{3},\sqrt{3}], compute the determinant of A and convert the condition \det A\ge0 into an explicit interval condition on n. You may also use that the 2\times2 principal minor \det\begin{pmatrix}2&n\\n&3\end{pmatrix}=6-n^2 must be nonnegative, although the final interval should come from the sharp determinant condition.
